config LIB_BOARD_CLOCK
    bool "Board clock: the DWT cycle counter extended to 64 bits"
    default n
    depends on CPU_CORTEX_M_HAS_DWT
    depends on SOC_FAMILY_STM32
    help
      The clock every board timestamp is taken from: the Cortex-M DWT cycle
      counter (CYCCNT), extended to 64 bits in software and kept counting
      through WFI idle. Unlike the tickless SysTick count behind
      k_cycle_get_64(), it loses no cycles when the system timer is
      reprogrammed. Selected by JerryCAN and by the drivers that stamp events.
